    "reference": "Existing tests, fixtures, historical verification runs and Auto expectations remain unchanged. New regional tests use literal signed origins and storage/transaction invariants, source words including quiet NaNs and IEEE values, plus old native/API/provider and paired actual-input regressions. No new ImageJ oracle acquisition or full regional rotation/Boolean equivalence is claimed.",
    "actual_ui": "Real keyboard input types Move X=-5 and Move Y=3 and pointer input clicks Apply in a single shared ImGui renderer lifetime. The regional saved row retains its complete frame while active/Previous selections remain independent. Twelve existing budget/pointer/modifier recipes run through both installed standalone C++ and Python launch paths; three additional standalone regressions also run. This is not OS-input or new regional standalone-launch certification.",
    "failed_attempts": "The first native patch inspected kind before its required-field preflight and leaked std::out_of_range on a malformed record. Its retained executable reproduces the error; reordering restores the invalid-wire contract, and the original 16 native cases/1600 checks pass. Initial new tests mistakenly classified a different valid intrinsic shape with the same packed length as malformed, used the wrong control diagnostics fields, and tried to retain a saved draft across renderer teardown. Only these new test assumptions were corrected; actual typing and Apply now share one renderer lifetime. One Linux launch occurred before helper synchronization finished, returned missing-script, and was started once the script existed. Final production/test sources were frozen before both qualified builds."
